    "fia_entry_exit_rules": "16.1 In accordance with Chapter 4, Articles 4 and 6 of Appendix L to the ISC drivers must\nfollow the procedures at pit entry and pit exit.\n16.2 Pertaining to Chapter IV Article 6c of Appendix L to the ISC, the “line painted on the track for\nthe purpose of separating cars leaving the pit lane from those on the track” is the line\nhighlighted in the image below using blue arrows. Thus, except during reconnaissance laps\nas described in Point 13.2 of these notes, no part of a tyre of a car exiting the pit lane may\ncross this line.\nFurthermore, except when passing a car which has stopped to perform a practice start during\na Free Practice Session as described in Point 13.1 of these notes, for the safety and orderly\nconduct of the event no part of a tyre of a car exiting the pit lane may cross the white line\npainted on the right-hand side of the Pit Exit Road as highlighted in the image below using\nred arrows. (new picture added).\nFor the avoidance of doubt, crossing means that the outside of any tyre should not go beyond\nthe outside, with respect to the Pit Exit Road, of these lines.\n16.3 Pertaining to Chapter 4, Article 4 of Appendix L to the ISC any driver passing on the left\nhand side of the junction of the dashed white line to the solid white line (as the image bellow)\nat the pit entry road will be considered as entering the pit lane",
